  "scope": "The command adapter now owns the production completion-count/name validation, native outcome/member checks, saturated item accounting and declaration-ordered value/terminal assembly. The VM retains full plan/binding admission, released BranchCompletion/BranchOutcome/Step types, continuation and failure validation, exact fault mapping, final value/encoding bounds and saved-binding completion. All outcomes are admitted before aggregate bounds and terminal selection; a stop cannot hide later invalid data and arrival order cannot select a different terminal. Frozen parity covers six admitted plan forms, nine outcome kinds per member, both arrival orders, five budgets and prefix/final modes, plus malformed plan/completion combinations. Exact results, faults, serialized bytes and input-plan bytes match. Direct VM-free consumers keep move-only local terminal/error pointer identity, release discarded ownership, preserve validation refusal order and use saturating counts. Existing default memory/SQLite group/capture/successor suites exercise the same migrated path including additional plan forms. The adapter requires a pre-admitted bounded plan and trusted validators; assembly is uncommitted data, not execution, authentic recovery or replay authority. No fuel construction, replacement evaluator, journal schema change or complete native durable recovery is claimed.",
